  "query_preview": "Outlook: Thursday - Weekend...\nBy the latter half of the week, western CONUS ridging will \namplify, fostering deeper downstream troughing over the Great \nLakes. This shift will place Central Illinois on the cooler side\nof the baroclinic zone, leading to a transition toward near- to\nslightly-below-normal temperatures. While the airmass will \nmoderate, the LLJ will continue to provide sufficient forcing to\nmaintain daily chances for showers and thunderstorms, \nparticularly during the evening and overnight periods.",
